;; FH-ROUTELINK-003 — the caller's :on-click runs first and may veto.
;;
;; A route-link with an analytics ping, a confirm dialog, or a
;; "you have unsaved changes" guard needs two things the framework cannot
;; guess: to run BEFORE the navigation decision, and to be able to stop
;; it. So `:on-click` is not merged, wrapped, or run after — it runs
;; first, and if it prevented the default the framework stands down and
;; the caller owns the outcome.
;;
;; Asserted in a real browser, because "prevented the default" is a
;; property of a real event object, and the ordering claim is only
;; meaningful against a real dispatch.
{:fh/id "FH-ROUTELINK-003"
 :fh/law
 "A caller-supplied :on-click runs before the framework's click decision and pre-empts it: if it prevents the default, the framework neither prevents nor dispatches."

 :routes {:fh.route/cart "/cart"}

 :cases
 [{:why           "a caller :on-click that does not veto — it runs, and the framework still intercepts"
   :props         {:to :fh.route/cart}
   :veto?         false
   :caller-ran?   true
   :dispatched?   true}
  {:why           "a caller :on-click that calls preventDefault — the framework stands down"
   :props         {:to :fh.route/cart}
   :veto?         true
   :caller-ran?   true
   :dispatched?   false}]

 ;; The caller runs before the decision, not after it: at the moment the
 ;; caller is invoked, nothing has been prevented yet.
 :ordering {:default-prevented-when-caller-runs false}}
